do_1 = "Decode the request event data as the kernel does: u64 requestId, u8 kind 1 or 2, u32 payloadLength > 0 and exactly that many payload bytes (src/modules/web/lx_web_intake.c:151-168); kind 3 is not an origin-2 kind (include/layerx/lx_web.h:24-25)."
do_2 = "Refuse a second request in one call with LXP_DUPLICATE_ENTRY (src/modules/programs/call.c:1883) and an id already pending or answered with LXP_SEQUENCE_REUSED (src/modules/programs/call.c:1888-1900)."
do_3 = "Sum the call's applied legs of one asset into that asset's web fee account; refuse a zero total with LXP_FEE_UNPAYABLE (src/modules/programs/call.c:1902-1903, src/modules/programs/call.c:1920) and a second asset with LXP_ASSET_MISMATCH (src/modules/programs/call.c:1911-1913); the asset must be listed in Params.ProgramFeeDenoms."
do_4 = "Write the 123-byte record in the byte order of web_request_record (src/modules/programs/call.c:1935-1954) under the key layout of web_pending_key (src/modules/programs/call.c:603-612), storing keccak256(payload) as the capture does (src/modules/programs/call.c:1921-1922)."
do_5 = "Read IsPaused first (modules/xweb/keeper/keeper.go:105-107) and refuse with LXP_XWEB_PAUSED; add the program store helpers beside the existing get and set helpers (modules/xweb/keeper/keeper.go:29-46)."
